<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Chapter 39 — Secrets Management.
    secret/   Secret (a value that doesn't leak through toString, logs or equals; wipeable) and MountedSecrets
              (a Kubernetes Secret volume followed through the kubelet's atomic ..data swaps)
    vault/    VaultClient (OpenBao / HashiCorp Vault HTTP API: Kubernetes login, KV v2, database credentials, leases)
              and DatabaseCredentials (renew until max_ttl, then rotate to new credentials before the old ones end)
    web/      order-service: configuration from OpenBao/Vault via Spring Cloud Vault, a HikariCP pool whose
              credentials come from a rotating Spring Vault lease (HikariCredentialsProvider)
  resources/openbao, eso and k8s hold the OpenBao policy and setup, External Secrets Operator resources, and the
  Kubernetes encryption-at-rest and pod configuration. verify/run.sh measures everything except web/ against a real
  OpenBao dev server and PostgreSQL 16.
-->
